<title>USA: Sioux Falls feeder cattle steady-up $3 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sioux Falls feeder cattle steady-up $3 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Receipts - This Week 2,410 Last Week 977 Last Year 1,660, USDA said.  Compared to last Thursday, feeder steers over 1000 lbs and heifers over 950 lbs sold steady to $1.00 per cwt higher; lighter weights $2.00-$3.00 higher. Offerings included many lots and loads attractive quality backgrounded steers and heifers as well as a moderate showing cattle off grass. Good demand. Good attendance farmer-feeder buyers. 93 percent over 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Steers - Medium and Large 1 - lot 549 lbs 96.20, lot 597 lbs 98.75, lot 630 lbs 82.75, part load 672 lbs 91.00, 700-750 lbs 82.00-88.00, 750-800 lbs 78.00-82.20, 800-850 lbs 76.50-79.00, 850-900 lbs 74.75- 78.00, 900-950 lbs 72.25-77.40, 950-1000 lbs 69.75-76.90, 1000-1050 lbs including some fleshy 68.75-74.30, 1050-1100 lbs including some fleshy 66.50-71.60, 1100-1150 lbs fleshy 68.30-69.50, load fleshy 1195 lbs 65.70.  Holstein - Large 2 - part load 429 lbs 83.00, 500-550 lbs 78.00- 80.75, lot 803 lbs 59.25, lot 870 lbs 62.00, 900-950 lbs 60.75-62.00, 1000-1050 lbs 61.50-62.00, lot 1091 lbs 59.85, 1150-1200 lbs 56.00- 58.50.</p>
<p>Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - part load 505 lbs 87.50, 600-650 lbs 80.90-83.50, small lot 698 lbs 74.50, 700-750 lbs 76.70-82.00, 750- 800 lbs 72.25-78.90, 800-850 lbs 69.00-75.90, 850-900 lbs 67.50-75.30, 900-950 lbs 67.00-72.50, 950-1000 lbs 67.40-69.00, fleshy 1000-1050 lbs 65.20-67.60, l050-1070 lbs fleshy 64.90.</p>
